## Capacity math — CORRECTED FORMULA

**required OC/day = forecast units / (productivity × 65)**  ← use this
~~demand/65 × (1 + (1 − productivity))~~ was wrong (1.26 vs correct 1/0.74 = **1.35**).

| Scenario | Demand | OC/day | Fits 24? |
|---|---:|---:|:--:|
| A. Do nothing (post ill will) | 525 | 10.9 | yes |
| B. Base forecast | 656 | 13.6 | yes |
| C. + Rio to 7-cap | 856 | 17.8 | yes |
| D. + full web rebuild | 1,171 | **24.3** | **no (barely)** |
| E. + NYC store | 1,571 | **32.7** | **no** |

- Ceiling = **1,154 units** (24 × 0.74 × 65). **CAPACITY IS NOW THE BINDING CONSTRAINT — not demand, not product.**
- **Idle cash fixes it:** $1,010,838 idle is what Asset Mgmt 0.353 punishes. A 4th printer ≈ **$240,000** (24% of cash) → 32/day / ~1,539 units. Rio+web+NYC needs ~33/day = **2 more printers**.
- **Ownership is NOT what burned us in Q2.** The $148,652 excess-capacity charge came from **SCHEDULING** unused OC. Ownership costs only depreciation (~$10k/qtr/printer). Q3 proof: owned 24, scheduled 8, paid $0 excess capacity.

